	<key>readme</key>
	<string>## Setup

Install Claude Code, run `claude` once in Terminal and log in with your Claude account. Messages then use your Claude plan, with no API key.

To pay per use instead, paste a Claude API key from the Claude Console into API Key. Claude Code still needs to be installed, but you don't need to log in.

Custom Instructions are standing instructions applied to every chat, such as the language or tone to use.

The workflow finds Claude Code by itself in the usual install locations. If it can't, run `which claude` in Terminal and paste the result into Claude Path.

## Usage

Launch the chat window with the `claude` keyword or the Hotkey. Type text after the keyword to start a new chat with it.

To use Claude from anywhere, select text or files and choose the Ask Claude Universal Action, or set the second Hotkey to send the current selection. Then pick a preset, such as Fix spelling and grammar or Summarise, and the chat opens with the answer on its way. Pick Ask Claude to open a chat with the text and type your own question.

In the chat window, choose a preset from the Presets menu (⌘P) and your next message is sent with it. Choose Edit Presets… there to add, change, reorder or delete presets. A preset can have its own model, and can paste its reply back automatically when used through Ask Claude.

The regenerate button (⌘R) asks the last question again and replaces the reply. ⌘⇧C copies the last reply.

Attach up to 10 files to a message with the paperclip, or press ⌘⇧V to attach what is on the clipboard: a screenshot, copied files or copied text. Images, PDFs, Office and iWork documents, text files and zip archives work. You can also run Ask Claude on files.

⌘⇧↩ pastes the last reply into the app you came from, replacing the text you had selected, and closes the chat window.

Each chat keeps its own Claude Code session, so follow-up questions have the full conversation. You can switch models between messages.

Search your chats with the box above the list (⌘F), right-click a chat to copy or delete it, and move between chats with ⌘] and ⌘[.</string>
